# Management

## REPL

An interactive terminal built into every entry node for real-time tunnel management. Use it to view peers, active connections, and traffic statistics, or to reconfigure routes on the fly.

Common commands include: `peers`, `connections`, `stats`, `route add`, and `route del`.

## REST API

An HTTP API for programmatic control. Use the API to query status, list peers, manage routes, and pull metrics. Enable the API with the `--api` flag.

{% codeblock code="wallhack entry --listen :443 --api 127.0.0.1:6566" /%}
